# A2-O3 final-pair private component proposal

Status: source-only, unparsed and unexecuted. Root alone selects/promotes/imports/runs this inert `.gd.txt`. No production, Git, queue, public evidence, mailbox, run or worker edits were made. No new runtime constructor hook is needed.

## Explicit authority boundary

`DeclaredFinalPair` extends the exact selected Canal production script. Its only combat behavior overrides are `_actor_stage_allowed` and `_actor_admission_allowed`, which declare the two final consumers initially eligible. This is a TEST constructor/context; it is **not** production progress or proof that the actual before-final checkpoint was committed. `_stage_index` remains zero, all defeat/pending/contact/checkpoint history remains empty, the real `_checkpoint_is_committed()` remains false, and earlier pockets remain alive with cycle0. Public parent snapshot, restore and progression requests explicitly refuse. The fixture does not assign stage3, create fake defeats, touch checkpoint state or reinterpret constructor-only evidence as whole-level acceptance.

Initial spawn is the earlier accepted focused final-pair feet `(0,.1,-21.8)`, supplied as a Marker before the sole production configure. Main receives the existing TEST public Challenge profile provider before entry. An actual enemy-free paused Main legally equips neutral `J0/P0/S0/WEAPON-01`, or one representative existing short/slow `J1/P2/S2/WEAPON-03`, before loading the component. Main's normal constructor creates its real shared Player at that marker and carries the legal kit. No post-entry Player pose, HP, ammo, clock, cooldown, actor position, phase, lease or proof write is made.

## Production code reused unchanged

The subclass inherits `_on_enter_level`, `_construct_arrangement`, `_physics_process`, `_update_actor_visibility`, `_activate_tool`, `_tool_context_live`, `_response_context`, `_ray_presentation_guard`, `_tool_presentation_guard`, `_handler_window`, `_proposal_framed`, `_proposal_preserves_running_responses`, `_candidate_preserves_running_views`, all original Scheduler/Ray/Lane code, floor/blocker/cues/camera/HUD and cleanup. The source runtime is pinned to `3b768398c9f975cac7a99ebfbd61455f3b86388521433775b9e7ed3c954c6c0b`; data to `0a7e3db98651d5d636f093935493278524a33db46bcc6bccd99ab07c9d44830c`.

All four actual native owners must remain bound: first_scout/final_scout to the original Scout actors, tool_second_handler/tool_final_handler to the actual Lanes. Unchanged first_scout(-.65,0,-3) and second_handler(.65,0,-12) remain idle and HP30. Fresh Challenge must select near final_handler(-.65,0,-21.2) and farther final_scout(.65,0,-23.5), preserving both recipients' own Y. Both original Handler Lanes must equal their own selected slot to slot+BACK*3.8, halfwidth.31, with the same low opening.

The driver reuses the accepted fixture's native120 barrier, `_wait_mixed_plan`, exact `_same_plan`, routed swipe, deliberate stop and immediate first-tap primary. Its copied `_follow_pair` differs only in name, diagnostic wording and removing the old TEST ammo=0 write/setup row. Original native segment starts, recovery/lock deadlines, normal readiness, exact complete cooldown and original full kit remain assertions. The first timely native armed ordinary response wins; the fixture does not delay a committed response while waiting for a preferred attacker. Both living final consumers must independently reach actual owner-bound armed ordinary proofs; a sampled overlap is reported without inventing a simultaneous-overlap gate. One real selected escape/return/ordinary-primary/full-cadence path is executed per declared kit; this is not two enemy defeats or an all-kit matrix.

## Minimal Root selection and execution

If Root accepts this source, copy only this draft to `tests/act2_o3_arrangement_component.gd`, add that exact file and its generated UID to the next frozen named cohort, and use the normal Godot queue. No extra parse engine phase is needed if the already necessary import/native launch compiles the new leaf. Proposed independent selectors are `--component-neutral` and `--component-short-slow`. Supply a fresh existing-directory `user://.../report.exact.json` through `CINDER_A2_O3_COMPONENT_REPORT`. These are proposed commands/selectors, not executed results; no exact count, timing or success is predicted.

Run neutral first. If a concrete failure occurs, preserve raw log/partial report/source maps and diagnose that failure before another scope. A decline caused by the unchanged source/view/held-response guard is evidence, never permission to weaken that guard. Do not re-run the old whole-prefix focused smoke just to generate this component. The independent new20 whole-Shell test supplies actual valid parent entry/Save/opposite-preference/fresh Continue/Retry/Leave protection; this component supplies no parent save evidence.

After appropriate headless evidence, one `--component-portrait` run uses the neutral component and the same actual proof/normal input path. At the actual timely native plan it publicly pauses, excludes the TEST menu, captures one actual540x1170 frame, compares full real Player/native Scheduler/Ray/Lane/actor/view packets plus input/camera/HUD/observed events before and after draw, then resumes without consuming a native tick. No parent snapshot is written or synthesized. Root must actually inspect the resulting pixels for Hero, both living sources, actionable footprint/opening, safe landing and reused dry floor; receipt `inspection` stays pending until then. Actual native view failure remains a failure. No OS focus bypass or automatic resume-on-focus path is enabled (`_capture` stays false).

Normal inherited level exit and Main disposal retire actual Hero/source/cue trees and weak references; the unique cached scene must also be released. The report contains real rows/counts/first_failure/complete, actual selected plan/actions/armed observations/phase samples, source subset before/after and an honest footer. Root's existing wrapper remains responsible for external queue/owned-child timeout/closure/raw diagnostics and immutable source maps, including failed/unexecuted attempts.

## Reused evidence and limits

Original A2-O3 acceptance remains accepted. Reuse the unchanged accepted first pockets, original loading/transitions/completion/contact and scoped transport evidence. Preserve original Root33/1 and owner failures, original labelled supported placements/injuries, and corrected43/0 cause/receipt. The existing pure/legacy/new20 Shell checks remain distinct. This draft does not establish production final-stage admission, a genuine before-final checkpoint, prior defeats, a route/clear/exit, both actual primary targets per kit, every timing/pose/gear, balance, performance, full art, mobile or release. Those untested behaviors do not gate the focused amendment.
